## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a privacy-conscious, low-latency analytics pipeline under multi-region constraints, with DP guarantees and drift detection.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time streaming with Kafka + Flink
- Differential privacy (epsilon ~1.0)
- Region-local state and windowed aggregations (<100 ms)
- Drift detection and observability
- Data residency and governance

## Code Example
```javascript
function addDPNoise(count, epsilon) {
  const sigma = Math.sqrt(2 / epsilon);
  const noise = randn_bm() * sigma;
  return Math.max(0, Math.round(count + noise));
}
function randn_bm() {
  let u = 0, v = 0;
  while (u === 0) u = Math.random();
  while (v === 0) v = Math.random();
  return Math.sqrt(-2.0 * Math.log(u)) * Math.cos(2 * Math.PI * v);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate privacy guarantees in production?
- What data contracts would you enforce with product teams to prevent over-collection?

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates your ability to design privacy-preserving, offline-first collaborative systems at scale. It tests technical understanding of cryptographic protocols, peer-to-peer networking, CRDT algorithms, and cost-benefit analysis while considering regulatory compliance and user experience constraints.

## Key Concepts

- Privacy-preserving collaborative editing
- CRDT convergence and conflict-free resolution
- Peer-to-peer mesh topology and infrastructure costs
- End-to-end encryption with lifecycle key management
- Compliance logging and audit trail requirements
- Performance trade-offs between latency and device resource consumption

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple OR-Set CRDT merge (illustrative)
function mergeORSet(A, B) {
  const merged = new Set([...A.added, ...B.added]);
  [...A.removed, ...B.removed].forEach(item => merged.delete(item));
  return merged;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
New angle on CBA: gating cross‑app features via an on‑device policy engine, balancing UX, energy, and safety with cloud updates.

## Key Concepts
- On‑device policy engines and gating rules
- Resource awareness (battery, thermal, memory)
- Telemetry footprint and privacy compliance
- Rollout strategy and break‑even analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
function shouldRunFeature(state, policy) {
  if (state.battery < 20) return false;
  if (state.temperature > 45) return false;
  if (state.freeMemory < 200) return false;
  return policy.allowsFeature;
}
```

