## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design a pragmatic CBA for on-device decision logic that changes user experience while preserving privacy and reducing server load. Tests modeling of energy, storage, and regulatory costs alongside rollout governance.

## Key Concepts

- On-device decisioning and privacy
- Compute and energy modeling
- Data minimization and consent logging
- Telemetry footprint and storage planning
- Rollout gates and break-even analysis

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo cost model for CBA
function cba(params) {
  const energy = params.cpuW * params.hours;
  const storage = params.rulesKB * params.devices / 1024;
  const savings = params.backendCostPerUnit * params.throughputReduction;
  const compliance = params.complianceCost;
  return energy + storage - savings + compliance;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate energy estimates across device SKUs?
- How would you adapt the model for regional regulatory differences?

